TWO DELIBERATE RESIDUES, both recorded so a later session does not read them as drift:
  1. flash:/default.cfg is 1714 B where the pre-campaign original was 1703 B. The 11-byte delta
     is `lldp run`, which bench_probe switches on and leaves on by design and which was in
     running-config before this case began. default.cfg was restored by RE-SAVING the
     torn-down running-config (F3 blocks a direct copy), so it is functionally equivalent, not
     byte-identical.
  2. flash:/precampaign.cfg (1703 B) is LEFT IN PLACE ON PURPOSE. It is the only byte-exact
     copy of the pre-campaign startup config, and tb277's /tmp does not survive a box reboot.
     It is an inert file and is NOT residue. Delete it only once the bench baseline is
     confirmed no longer needed.

