VERDICT: PASS -- a named hardware IP ACL bound to the static LAG `sa1` enforces correctly on
both members, with host and network source/destination forms, with and without the vlan
qualifier, first-match ordering, non-IP (ARP) traffic unaffected, equally via `access-group`
and via `service-policy input`, surviving a reload, and removing cleanly with no config or
TCAM residue. The stack-straddle and stack-failover clauses in ck.db's steps_text were
withdrawn by the Test Engineer and were NOT run.
